hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"172","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace “He performed ablution and washed his face three times, his hands twice, and his feet twice, and wiped his head,” and he saw that he said: and he scattered"
"173","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us that Malik told him, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya Al-Mazini, on the authority of his father, He said to Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was the grandfather of Amr bin Yahya: Did Can you show me how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution? Abdullah bin Zaid said: Yes. So he called for ablution, emptied his hands, washed his hands twice, then rinsed his mouth and rinsed his hands three times, then washed them. His face three times, then he washed his hands twice, up to the elbows, then he wiped his head with his hands, then he faced them and turned back, starting with the introduction. His head, then he took them to the back of his head, then returned them until he returned to the place from which he started, then he washed his feet.” Malik said: This is the most comprehensive wiping and the one I love most."
